+## Acceptance failures (10) — DOM identity defects
+
+An external Cypress acceptance suite reports 10 failures. All share the same root cause:
+the `render()` function in `js/app.js` calls `todoList.innerHTML = ''` on every state change,
+destroying all DOM nodes. A real browser's Cypress holds references to elements before the
+action; after `render()` replaces them, those references are detached.
+
+The in-harness suite (happy-dom) passes because it re-queries the DOM fresh each step.
+
+**Fix: mutate DOM nodes in place instead of rebuilding the list.**
+- Toggle/toggle-all/clear-completed: toggle classes and properties on the existing `<li>`
+  elements instead of calling `render()`.
+- Editing: toggle the `editing` class on the existing `<li>` instead of calling `render()`.
+  The `render()` function should only run for initial render and structural changes
+  (add/remove items).
+
