+  Rule: DOM identity
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves the element reference
+    Given the todo list has 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    When I capture a reference to the first todo element
+    And I click the toggle checkbox on the todo
+    Then the captured reference is still attached to the DOM
+    And the captured reference has class "completed"
+    And the toggle checkbox inside the captured reference is checked
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking a todo preserves the element reference
+    Given the todo list has 1 completed item with title "Buy milk"
+    When I capture a reference to the first todo element
+    And I click the toggle checkbox on the todo
+    Then the captured reference is still attached to the DOM
+    And the captured reference does not have class "completed"
+    And the toggle checkbox inside the captured reference is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all preserves all element references
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Buy eggs", "Buy bread"
+    When I capture references to all todo elements
+    And I click the "toggle-all" checkbox
+    Then each captured reference is still attached to the DOM
+    And each captured reference has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed preserves remaining element references
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Buy eggs", "Buy bread"
+    And the todo titled "Buy milk" is completed
+    And the todo titled "Buy eggs" is completed
+    When I capture references to all todo elements
+    And I click the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the captured references for remaining items are still attached to the DOM
+    And the captured references for completed items are detached from the DOM
+
+  Scenario: Entering edit mode preserves the element reference
+    Given the todo list has 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    When I capture a reference to the first todo element
+    And I double-click the todo label
+    Then the captured reference is still attached to the DOM
+    And the captured reference has class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Edit input is visible when editing
+    Given the todo list has 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the todo label
+    Then the edit input is visible
+    And the view is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit preserves the element reference
+    Given the todo list has 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    When I capture a reference to the first todo element
+    And I double-click the todo label
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic milk"
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then the captured reference is still attached to the DOM
+    And the captured reference does not have class "editing"
+    And the label inside the captured reference has title "Buy organic milk"
+
+  Scenario: Cancelling an edit preserves the element reference
+    Given the todo list has 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    When I capture a reference to the first todo element
+    And I double-click the todo label
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy organic milk"
+    And I press Escape in the edit input
+    Then the captured reference is still attached to the DOM
+    And the captured reference does not have class "editing"
+    And the label inside the captured reference has title "Buy milk"
+
